  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strategic Partnership between the FCDO and the European Institute of Peace</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Partnership between the FCDO&#x2019;s Conflict Resolution Department and the European Institute of Peace with a focus on strengthening European involvement and collaboration in two contexts: Sudan and China. The goal is to explore and deepen UK-EU collaboration on peace and security initiatives, enabling joined-up engagements that respond to the critical challenges the continent faces in conflict prevention and resolution. This will also provide the FCDO with privileged access to the Institute&#x2019;s network both in European capitals, Brussels and conflict actors in the field. The Institute proposes to make good use of this existing partnership with the EU, to further UK-EU conversations and action on concrete mediation and dialogue opportunities. Building on context-tailored approaches, the Institute proposes to work with FCDO through in-depth partnership through two activities: Activity 1: A Pathway to Enhanced European Collaboration on Sudan (phase I). 
Activity 2: Trilateral Dialogue between China, Europe and the US.</narrative>
  </description>
